cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "numopt: classical one-dimensional numerical optimization methods"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Tapias Zarrazola"
    given-names: "John Edisson"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5166-0679"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kemquiros/optimizacion"
abstract: >-
  Tested implementations of golden-section search, bisection on the derivative,
  Newton-Raphson, deterministic and stochastic gradient descent, and the
  conjugate gradient method. Every routine returns the full iterate history so
  that convergence can be inspected rather than asserted. Originally written for
  the undergraduate course Optimizacion at Universidad de Antioquia (2017) and
  rewritten as a library in 2026.
keywords:
  - optimization
  - numerical methods
  - golden section search
  - conjugate gradient
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
